# Engineering principles

## Prefer ready-made, proven solutions

- Use official docs and MCP (Context7, Supabase, Vercel) for library/API questions
- Prefer maintained npm packages over custom implementations (auth, UI, validation, email)
- Match project stack: Next.js App Router, Prisma, PostgreSQL, Docker — do not add parallel stacks

## Verify, do not invent

- Never fabricate: API endpoints, env variable names, CLI flags, package exports, file paths
- Confirm in codebase (`grep`, `read`) or official documentation before using
- Do not claim deploy/tests passed without actually running them
- If blocked (missing password, tool, access) — state it clearly

## Complex tasks workflow

1. Check `docs/ROADMAP.md` scope
2. Research existing solution (docs/MCP)
3. Minimal integration into `src/` or `prisma/`
4. Verify with build or runtime check
